## Fallback & Resilience Behavior

### Local-Only Fallback Mode

Triggered when:
- Initial RTDB read fails (permission denied, offline, etc.)
- Write operation fails

**State Management:**
- `isUsingLocalFallback = true` flag set
- All mutations remain in-memory only
- State changes still fire UI subscribers
- No persistence to RTDB until connection restored

**Recovery:**
- Next successful read from RTDB rehydrates full state
- `isUsingLocalFallback = false` flag cleared
- Local changes **discarded** (not merged with DB state)

